      "summary": "GlobalFoundries and TSMC Partner on US Interposer Production for CoWoS Electronics For You BUSINESS",
      "body": "Five-year agreement expands Malta, New York fab to create domestic supply chain for high-performance AI chips.\nGlobalFoundries (GF) has reached an agreement with TSMC to supply silicon interposers for TSMC’s Chip-on-Wafer-on-Substrate (CoWoS) advanced packaging ecosystem from a US manufacturing base.\nUnder the initial five-year contract, GF will act as a foundry partner to TSMC, adding interposer manufacturing capacity at its principal fabrication facility in Malta, New York. The partnership establishes the first domestic US supply source for silicon interposers—a critical component in advanced 2.5D and 3D packaging that integrates embedded deep trench capacitors to enhance thermal and power efficiency in high-performance computing and AI accelerators.\nHighlighting the supply chain impact, Ed Kaste, Senior Vice President of the CMOS Business Unit at GlobalFoundries, stated: “Advanced packaging is becoming increasingly critical to delivering the performance, power efficiency and scale r",
